2026-11-08 — Setup verified before launch.
  Ports swept after 14.15 and still clean: ARD 3283, Docker 3307, Ollama 49290 only.
  Six arms built from `work/20/20.2/setup.py` — arm names, an arm filter and the overwrite
  guard the only edits. The blanket `rmtree` 15.4 paid for is left in the file behind
  `if False:` so the next reader sees what was removed.
  **Two inherited-instrument traps caught before launch, both from copying 20.2's scorers:**
   - `mutate.py`'s `EDITS` is per-arm SQL lifted from what 20.2's arms wrote. Renaming the keys
     carried them onto arms whose code does not exist yet, where the mutation would have been
     applied to the wrong source or silently reported `n/a` on arms whose tests were never
     exercised. **Blanked; filled only after the arms run.**
   - `score.py`'s `AGENT` map points at 20.2's transcripts. Renamed, it would have scored the
     wrong agents. **Blanked.**
  **The validation check itself was wrong twice and is recorded that way.**
   - First attempt diffed the live `r202` trees. Those arms have since done their work, so the
     diff showed their scoreboards, not the seed. Corrected to compare each tree **at its own
     setup commit**.
   - Second attempt read file contents as text and died on a binary file. Corrected to compare
     **git blob hashes**: same name and same hash is byte-identical with no decoding.
  Result → `03b_delta.txt`: S seed vs 20.2's P seed, 726 files each, **differing only on
  `BEMYAGENT.md`** — 19.5's Step 0 line, which cannot fire on a populated `.bemyagent/`.
  O seed vs 20.2's N seed, 10 files each, **no difference at all**. S vs S and O vs O identical.
  All three O arms hold no `BEMYAGENT.md`, no `.bemyagent/`, no `CLAUDE.md`, no `AGENTS.md`.
  Both prompts stored verbatim before launch, byte-identical to 20.2's.
